@startuml option_b_lite_static_kg
title Option B-lite — static KG content in system prompt

actor User
participant "ask.py\n(CLI)" as CLI
participant "LangGraph\nagent loop" as Agent
participant "KG context loader\n(loads once at startup)" as Loader
participant "LLM\n(Gemini)" as LLM
participant "MCP server" as MCP
participant "Fusion tools" as FusionTools
participant "OracleClient" as OracleClient
participant "FusionClient" as FusionClient
participant "Oracle 26ai\n(SPIRE)" as Oracle
participant "Fusion REST" as FusionPod

== Startup (once per agent process) ==
Agent -> Loader : load_kg_context()
Loader -> OracleClient : SELECT * FROM kg_entity
Loader -> OracleClient : SELECT * FROM kg_edge
Loader -> OracleClient : SELECT * FROM kg_pattern
Loader -> OracleClient : SELECT * FROM kg_vocabulary
OracleClient -> Oracle : SQL × 4
Oracle --> OracleClient : all rows
OracleClient --> Loader : full KG
Loader -> Loader : format as system_prompt section
Loader --> Agent : static_kg_context (string)

== Per-request ==
User -> CLI : reference prompt
CLI -> Agent : run_agent(prompt)
Agent -> MCP : load_mcp_tools()
MCP --> Agent : Fusion tools only

Agent -> LLM : SYSTEM = base_prompt + static_kg_context\nUSER = prompt
note right of LLM
  KG knowledge is always
  in the system prompt.
  Same content every request.
  LLM sees it whether or not
  the prompt needs it.
end note

LLM --> Agent : tool_call: search_suppliers_by_country("US")
Agent -> MCP : invoke
MCP -> FusionTools : ...
FusionTools -> FusionClient : GET /suppliers
FusionClient -> FusionPod : HTTPS
FusionPod --> FusionClient : 25 suppliers
FusionClient --> FusionTools : 25 suppliers
FusionTools --> MCP : 25 suppliers
MCP --> Agent : 25 suppliers
Agent -> LLM : updated context

note over LLM, Agent
  More Fusion calls follow.
  No KG queries during the run.
end note

LLM --> Agent : final_answer
Agent --> CLI : answer text
CLI --> User : printed answer
@enduml